WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.579
Adobe Creative Cloud can support eLearning by helping teams produce polished, reusable,

00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:05.698
accessible media assets.

00:00:05.698 --> 00:00:09.804
Those assets may include visuals, diagrams, narration, video, motion graphics, documents,

00:00:09.804 --> 00:00:12.416
job aids, and exports for course delivery.

00:00:12.416 --> 00:00:17.268
The tools support production, but they do not replace instructional purpose, audience analysis,

00:00:17.268 --> 00:00:18.388
or learning design.

00:00:18.388 --> 00:00:22.120
Strong eLearning production starts with objectives, storyboards, scripts, narration plans,

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.360
visual clarity, accessibility, review, and maintainability.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.092
When those pieces are clear, production tools become more effective.

00:00:28.092 --> 00:00:32.571
Designers can create the right asset in the right format instead of

00:00:32.571 --> 00:00:35.930
producing media simply because the tool makes it possible.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.781
The goal is not to use every application, every effect, or every format.

00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:45.633
The goal is to create learning materials that learners can understand, complete, apply,

00:00:45.633 --> 00:00:46.380
and revisit.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:48.992
A clean diagram, a clear narration track,

00:00:48.992 --> 00:00:53.471
or a practical job aid may be more valuable than a complex

00:00:53.471 --> 00:00:56.084
animation if it supports the objective better.

00:00:56.084 --> 00:00:57.950
Durable production depends on organization.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:02.428
Keep source files, exports, scripts, captions, review notes, and final packages traceable.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:04.668
Use naming conventions and version discipline.

00:01:04.668 --> 00:01:06.907
Test media in the course environment.

00:01:06.907 --> 00:01:11.759
A course that is easy to update will survive policy changes, brand updates,

00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:13.625
and future revisions more gracefully.

00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:16.984
The practical takeaway is simple: media should serve learning.

00:01:16.984 --> 00:01:21.836
Creative Cloud can help make course assets clearer, more consistent, and more professional.

00:01:21.836 --> 00:01:26.688
But every asset should be tied to a learner need, a course objective,

00:01:26.688 --> 00:01:28.181
or a workplace task.

00:01:28.181 --> 00:01:31.540
That is what turns production work into useful eLearning.
